Here is the semantic interpretation of the scene based on the provided ontology:

### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "FoggyUrbanIntersection" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :foggyCondition ;
    :hasRisk :occlusionRisk ;
    :hasRisk :rearEndCollisionRisk ;
    :hasEvidence :evidence1 .

:foggyCondition a :FoggyCondition ;
    :description "Heavy fog reducing visibility to < 20 meters" .

:evidence1 a :FallingObjectIndicator ;
    :description "Fog density and depth suggest extreme visibility reduction" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :occlusionRisk .

:occlusionRisk a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Fog-induced occlusion of other vehicles and pedestrians" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.92"^^xsd:float .

:rearEndCollisionRisk a :RearEndCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility increases risk of rear-end collision with vehicle ahead" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.88"^^xsd:float .

:vehicle1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Vehicle ahead in foggy intersection" .

:vehicle2 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Ego vehicle in foggy intersection" .
```

### Identified Risks for each risk class

**Risk 1:**
Description: Fog-induced occlusion of other vehicles and pedestrians
Severity Score: 0.92

